taktuk
------------------------------------------
TakTuk is a tool for deploying parallel remote executions of commands to a
potentially large set of remote nodes. It spreads itself using an adaptive
algorithm and sets up an interconnection network to transport commands and
perform I/Os multiplexing/demultiplexing. The TakTuk mechanics dynamically
adapt to environment (machine performance and current load, network contention)
by using a reactive work-stealing algorithm that mixes local parallelization
and work distribution.

Runtime requirements:
  cygwin-3.6.12-1
  libtaktuk-devel-3.7.8-1bl1
  libtaktuk3-3.7.8-1bl1
  perl-5.44.0-1
  perl_base-5.44.0-1
  pkg-config-3.0.10-1

Build requirements:
(besides corresponding -devel packages)
  autoconf-20260320-3
  automake-20260320-2
  binutils-2.47-1
  cygport-0.37.12-1
  gcc-core-14.4.0-1
  libtool-2.6.2-1
  make-4.4.1-2

Canonical website:
  https://taktuk.gitlabpages.inria.fr/

Canonical download:
  https://gitlab.inria.fr/taktuk/taktuk/-/archive/version-3.7.8/taktuk-version-3.7.8.tar.gz

-------------------------------------------

Build instructions:
  1. unpack taktuk-3.7.8-X-src.tar.xz
  2. if you use setup to install this src package,
     it will be unpacked under /usr/src automatically
        % cd /usr/src
        % cygport ./taktuk-3.7.8-X.cygport all

This will create:
  /usr/src/taktuk-3.7.8-X-src.tar.xz
  /usr/src/taktuk-3.7.8-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libtaktuk3-3.7.8-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libtaktuk-devel-3.7.8-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/perl-taktuk-3.7.8-X.tar.xz

-------------------------------------------

